# MC-B-F2, the gated variant. L §5.18 Partial answers: "A rounding, min, max, a band, a comparison or a product of two
# holes meeting a hole makes the line a plain hole naming every hole." The spending move's `when sp[m] != none` is a
# comparison meeting the March hole, so the movement's existence is a hole (L §5.14) and the balance is a plain hole.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
source s "s"
place w: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 2025-01-01..
input sp[m in months]: money DUK question "spent?"

version o
  cite s
  known 2025-01-01
  opening[w] = 100.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  sp[*] = none "the other months"
  sp[2025-03] = ?"What was spent in March?" "March"

move spent[m in months]: transfers
  on end_of(m) - 1
  when sp[m] != none
  leg cash from w to shop amount sp[m]

ask q: bal(w, 2025-12-31) law 2025-12-31 partial
=== expect
q: ?"What was spent in March?" (sp[2025-03])
  law date 2025-12-31, cut 2026-01-01
